# Chezmoi source edits from Claude

Host `{{ .chezmoi.hostname }}` ({{ .profile | lower }} profile). What chezmoi manages is in `~/AGENTS.md`;
the commit-and-push policy is in shared-global.md. These are the Claude-only mechanics:

- Sessions rooted in `~/.local/share/chezmoi` run a PostToolUse hook (that repo's
  `.claude/settings.json`) that commits and pushes every Edit/Write/NotebookEdit there. Don't
  commit those again. Bash edits (`sed`, `git mv`, scripts) and sessions rooted anywhere else
  are not covered: commit and push them yourself, staging only your paths.
- Background jobs must run with cwd `~/.local/share/chezmoi` to edit source via Edit/Write:
  Claude Code's background worktree isolation is off (`worktree.bgIsolation: none`) only in that
  repo's `.claude/settings.json`. From `~` the edits land in a worktree `chezmoi apply` never reads.
